# Extra packages for the desktop edition, copied into
# config/package-lists/desktop.list.chroot by auto/config. The desktop itself
# (compositor, shell, portals) comes from the fellowship-desktop .deb that
# desktop/build.sh makes.

# Wayland session and GPU/software rendering. QEMU's virtio-gpu falls back to
# llvmpipe when 3D isn't passed; on real hardware and virgl guests Mesa picks
# the native driver, Vulkan ICD and VA-API video acceleration.
libegl-mesa0
libgl1-mesa-dri
libglx-mesa0
mesa-vulkan-drivers
mesa-va-drivers
intel-media-va-driver
xkb-data
dbus
# chvt: the session switches the screen to its own console, which the live
# image's autologin does not necessarily leave active
kbd

# Hardware firmware (non-free-firmware): Wi-Fi, GPU microcode, Realtek NICs
# and modern Intel SOF laptop audio. Unused in QEMU, required on bare metal.
firmware-linux
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-amd-graphics
firmware-intel-graphics
firmware-realtek
firmware-sof-signed

# Portals: the frontend, and the GTK backend for the file picker and friends.
# The Settings (colour-scheme) interface is answered by fellowship-portal.
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk

# Sound and media codecs: PipeWire with WirePlumber, RTKit for realtime
# scheduling, Pulse compatibility, and GStreamer plugins for media playback.
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
rtkit
gstreamer1.0-plugins-base
gstreamer1.0-plugins-good
gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad
gstreamer1.0-libav
gstreamer1.0-pipewire
# notify-send: the small client every desktop has for scripts and tests.
libnotify-bin

# Networking, power, printing, Bluetooth, firewall and session security:
# greetd + cage + accountsservice provide the graphical login screen;
# NetworkManager handles Wi-Fi/Ethernet; UPower reports battery/AC; mate-polkit
# answers admin prompts for Settings; gnome-keyring provides Secret Service;
# xwayland prepares X11 app compatibility; CUPS + system-config-printer handle
# printing; ufw gives a default-deny desktop firewall.
greetd
cage
accountsservice
network-manager
wpasupplicant
nm-connection-editor
upower
mate-polkit
gnome-keyring
libpam-gnome-keyring
libsecret-tools
xwayland
cups
system-config-printer
printer-driver-cups-pdf
bluez
blueman
ufw

# Look: fonts, icons and pointer the shell and the apps ask for.
# DejaVu alone leaves whole scripts with no glyphs, measured on the seat
# 2026-11-15: Arabic renders (DejaVu covers it), CJK draws tofu boxes and
# emoji has no colour glyphs. Noto core is 42 MB across 2 packages and the
# colour emoji font 11 MB in 1.
# `fonts-noto-cjk` is 54 MB downloaded and 89 MB installed — Chris's rule was
# that the installed footprint is the number that counts, and 54 MB is not
# 91 MB added to every install, so it is in. No image size budget is written
# down anywhere in either repository; the desktop image was 1.39 GB before
# this and lands near 1.45 GB, which fits a 4 GB stick with room to spare.
fonts-dejavu-core
fonts-urw-base35
fonts-noto-core
fonts-noto-color-emoji
fonts-noto-cjk
adwaita-icon-theme
breeze-icon-theme
breeze-cursor-theme

# The folders a desktop is expected to have. Nothing else creates them in
# this session: Debian's own hook sits in /etc/xdg/autostart, which the
# compositor deliberately does not read until FellowshipOS ships its own
# system autostart, so `fellowship-session` runs the updater at login. The
# screenshot path reads the file this writes, and Nemo's sidebar and
# Rhythmbox's library assume the folders exist.
xdg-user-dirs

# Drives and network shares in Strider (the file manager) go through GIO:
# GVfs's backends for SMB, SFTP, FTP and WebDAV and for browsing the
# network, its FUSE bridge so a mounted share is an ordinary folder that
# copy, move and undo work on, and UDisks for USB drives, with polkit's
# daemon so UDisks lets the person at the desktop open a drive (without it
# every mount was "not authorized", seen in the VM on 2026-11-19). Avahi lets
# Strider find FellowshipNAS machines by their _fellowship-nas._tcp advert,
# and nss-mdns resolves their .local names. The 1.0 image had none of the
# network pieces: Nemo didn't pull them in.
gvfs-backends
gvfs-fuse
udisks2
polkitd
avahi-daemon
libnss-mdns
# The everyday apps chosen in the desktop checklist: GTK 3 where there is a
# choice, so the session's GTK theme reaches them.
foot
mousepad
nemo
ristretto
atril
engrampa
qalculate-gtk
mpv
chromium
rhythmbox
zenity
